   \begin{align*}
   \text{angle } BAD &= 70 \\
   \text{angle } DAC &= 50 \\
   \text{angle } CAE &= 30
   \end{align*}

Let's look at the relationship between $A$ and $E$, the two ends of the diameter of the circle. We can see that triangle $ADE$ is a right triangle.

We have:
\[ \text{angle } ADE = 90 \]

Also, since the line $DE$ is a diameter of the circle, the angle subtended by the diameter at the circumference is 90 degrees:
\[ \text{angle } DEC = 90 \]

Now consider the quadrilateral $DECO$. Since the angles at $D$ and $C$ are both 90 degrees, and $O$ is the center of the circle, we can find the angle $DEO$:
